"""MEMBER A. Synthetic labelled training messages, generated by code (seeded, reproducible, declared in README).

The organisers' Data tab allows synthetic data. Nothing here is derived from test.csv: every template was written by
hand from the official labelling guide (classes, priority order, technique/action conventions).

Labels follow the guide:
  label   0 legit, 1 MFS/OTP/credential, 2 prize, 3 fake job/investment, 4 parcel phishing, 5 promo spam
  T1 organisation/role claimed as sender   T2 credential request   T3 payment demand
  T4 reward/prize lure   T5 urgency/threat/pressure   T6 unrealistic earning
  action 0 none, 1 hand over credentials/personal details, 2 pay/send money, 3 open a link,
         4 install an app / join a group / do tasks, 5 call / WhatsApp / contact a number

Template mini-language: "TECHS|ACTION|text". {S:kind} = claimed sender (adds T1), other {slot}s are filled at random.
generate(n, seed) returns a DataFrame text,label,techniques,action with registers (SMS, conversation, call transcript,
group chat, email/notice), languages (English, Banglish, Bangla) and hard negatives (warnings that quote scams).
"""
